# Type chips / filled tags — no all-caps

Any **project type** or **article type** label that sits on a chip fill（套底）must **not** use `text-transform: uppercase`.

Applies to:

- `.insight-chip` / `.insight-chip--on-media`
- `.project-type-chip` / `.project-type-chip--on-media`
- `.project-case-demo__tag`
- Any future filled type pill on covers or cards

Show the authored label as-is (e.g. `End-to-End Projects`), with normal sentence/title casing — never CSS-forced ALL CAPS.

On **dark surfaces** (`.insights-page`, `.insight-detail`, `.projects-page`), chip fill must use light-on-dark colors — default chip ink is for light backgrounds and will disappear on black.

# Insight label tokens (size / tracking for non-chip microcopy)

Shared tokens on `.insights-page` and `.insight-detail` for date / eyebrows / filter microcopy (not forced-uppercase chips):

- `--insight-label-tracking: 0.08em`
- `--insight-label-size: clamp(0.625rem, 0.58rem + 0.2vw, 0.75rem)`
- `--insight-meta-gap: 1.75rem`

Do not invent a different letter-spacing or font-size for those micro-labels on one Insights surface and another.
